From: oplus-sukisu_kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: adapt the BORE hunks that reject on 6.12.23

bore_6.12.patch is written against 6.12.44+. Two of its hunks do not apply
to OnePlus's sm8850 16.0.0 tree (6.12.23):

1. __pick_eevdf() still carries the older run-to-parity form

	if (sched_feat(RUN_TO_PARITY) && curr && protect_slice(curr))
		return curr;

   instead of the 6.12.44+ form

	if (curr && protect && protect_slice(curr))
		return curr;

2. update_curr() calls update_min_vruntime() right after update_deadline(),
   so the trailing context of the burst-accounting hunk does not match.

This patch re-applies both hunks against the 6.12.23 shapes. The inserted
code is identical to what bore_6.12.patch inserts; only the surrounding
context differs.

The build applies this only when kernel/sched/fair.c.rej exists, and only
after the main BORE patch has run with --fuzz=0.

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -1004,6 +1004,10 @@
 		curr = NULL;
 
 	if (sched_feat(RUN_TO_PARITY) && curr && protect_slice(curr))
+#ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
+		if (!(likely(sched_bore) && likely(sched_burst_parity_threshold) &&
+			sched_burst_parity_threshold < cfs_rq->nr_running))
+#endif // CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
 		return curr;
 
 	/* Pick the leftmost entity if it's eligible */
@@ -1325,6 +1329,12 @@
 	if (unlikely(delta_exec <= 0))
 		return;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
+	if (se_bore(curr)) {
+		se_bore(curr)->burst_time += delta_exec;
+		update_burst_penalty(curr);
+	}
+#endif // CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
 	curr->vruntime += calc_delta_fair(delta_exec, curr);
 	resched = update_deadline(cfs_rq, curr);
 	update_min_vruntime(cfs_rq);
